course: dictionary
lesson: 11020
title: The watt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A watt is a unit that measures power. Power tells you how fast energy is used or made. One watt is one joule of energy every second.
explain: The word watt is also a name. «James Watt greatly improved the steam engine; he did not invent it, as earlier steam engines already pumped water out of mines.» The sentence gives you a clue: he made something better that already existed, so the watt is named after a man who worked on engines.
explain: Look at the numbers around the word to find its meaning. A 60-watt bulb uses more power than a 10-watt bulb. So a bigger number of watts means a device is more powerful.
fact: A watt is a unit of power, which is joules of energy used or made each second.
fact: «Watt» is also a name: James Watt was a Scottish engineer who improved the steam engine.
fact: A kettle may use 3,000 watts, which is the same as 3 kilowatts.
fact: A kilowatt is 1,000 watts, and a megawatt is one million watts.
fact: Choosing devices with fewer watts, and switching them off when not in use, saves energy.
exercise: What is a watt a unit of? | Weight | *Power | Length | Time spent
exercise: A 10-watt bulb and a 60-watt bulb are both switched on. Which one uses more power? | *The 60-watt bulb | Neither uses any power | They use the same power | The 10-watt bulb
exercise: «James Watt greatly improved the steam engine; he did not invent it.» What did James Watt do to the steam engine? | *Improved it | Sold it at a shop | Invented it from nothing | Painted it
test: «A kettle uses 3,000 watts.» How many kilowatts is that? | 300 kilowatts | *3 kilowatts | 30 kilowatts
test: What is one watt, in words? | One joule of energy every hour | Ten joules of energy every minute | One joule of energy every metre | *One joule of energy every second
exam: Which choice saves the most energy? | *Choosing devices with fewer watts and switching them off | Leaving every light on all day | Buying devices with more watts | Buying the biggest kettle you can find
